meta {
  name: Fit firewall rules to an account
  type: http
  seq: 44
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/organizations/{{organization_id}}/firewall-rules/fit
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
}

docs {
  The rules of a firewall (`firewall`, its id) or a template (`template`, a slug or a custom template’s id) as the account `provider_credential_id` would hold them, at whichever provider. `changes` names every rule that does not arrive as it was — an outbound rule at an inbound-only provider, a protocol the provider does not take, a rule only its own provider understands — and why. `creatable` says whether the account can create a firewall of its own. Nothing is changed.

  Scope: `cloud.read`
}
